his is the Core prerequisite for PR48’s separate typed migration SDK 0.5.7; UMF retains inert meaning and plans, Weft handles SQL lowering, and the host retains execution authority.\n\nThe current source is `a1b909d4f92da6604aeb21d3ea60e9a9943a7f87`, based on `f5f4b7dbef12a757bc0bba6ae2f581998fe50dba`. It checks the complete authored 24-record catalog, returns bounded closed limit reasons for action-runtime failures, and isolates the source-DBAPI Rust component store with explicit rustfmt provisioning while retaining Rust 1.90.0 and the existing native assertions. The macOS artifact was built at `f4d22c6f0f9e308439e3646117e31239cf48bc07`; its full source tree matches a1b’s tree, and its producer identity remains distinct.\n\nCurrent direct and sdist-rebuilt Linux and macOS artifacts each passed 254 installed-artifact tests with zero skips. The raw Linux wheel is retained as evidence, not a publishable file. The repaired `manylinux_2_34_x86_64` wheel `umf_core-0.10.2-cp311-abi3-manylinux_2_34_x86_64.whl` passed [hosted qualification run 40359647952](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/umf/actions/runs/40359647952) with 254 tests and independent artifact review; its native digest matches the qualified Linux binary. This result is limited to that exact wheel and policy tag.\n\nCurrent normal PR checks report 62 successful checks, one expected skip, and one macOS Python 3.12 gate still running. Merge and publication remain held for that gate and the remaining release workflow. PR50 must be integrated through normal main-branch review before creating `python-v0.10.2`; release and PyPI upload use the Actions-only exact-tag workflow, followed by fresh public download and installed-wheel verification. No local registry upload is part of this process.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-24T03:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T16:56:59Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T16:56:59Z","merged_at":"2026-10-26T16:56:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"3fd8c61